{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"CORRECTION — my triage table said three members had 'no library helper, use raw PUT'. That was WRONG,\nand the plan is now library-first throughout.\n\nWE DO USE pycontribs/jira DIRECTLY, and always have. Every method in the DC transport goes through it:\nclient.create_issue, .issue, .assign_issue, .transitions, .transition_issue, .search_issues,\n.add_comment, .comments, .create_issue_link. There is NO hand-rolled REST in that file — the only\n'requests' import is for exception TYPES (the SSLError-vs-ConnectionError classification from 9fd4).\nHand-rolling a rest_client.py was PR #120's approach, which this epic rejected.\n\nMY ERROR: I enumerated jira.JIRA (189 public methods) and concluded set_parent/remove_label/\nset_reporter had no helper. The library's API is SPLIT across jira.JIRA and jira.resources.Issue, and\nIssue.update(fields=..., update=...) covers all three:\n    set_parent (sub-task) -> issue.update(fields={'parent': {'key': ...}})\n    remove_label          -> issue.update(update={'labels': [{'remove': ...}]})\n    set_reporter          -> issue.update(fields={'reporter': {'name': ...}})\nSo ALL TWELVE are reachable through the library; none needs raw REST.\n\nTHIS IS THE SAME MISTAKE J6 SHIPPED AS A BUG, and our own code documents it. From add_label's\ndocstring (transport.py:273): 'add_field_value lives on the ISSUE resource, not on the client:\njira.JIRA has no such attribute (verified against jira 3.10.5), so the earlier client-level call raised\nAttributeError on every invocation — this method could never have worked. It shipped because it had no\ntest at any tier.' I scanned the same half of the same API and reached the same wrong conclusion, in a\nplan whose whole purpose is fixing that class of defect.\n\nTwo further refinements this surfaces:\n * get_comments and get_issue_by_rest are missing SURFACE, not missing capability — the transport\n   ALREADY calls client.comments (:327) inside get_comment_map and client.issue (:234) inside\n   get_issue. They are trivial exposures.\n * That weakens my earlier 'the library shaped our gaps' hypothesis. The library provides a helper for\n   effectively all of them, so the gaps are not library-shaped — they are ORACLE-shaped. We implemented\n   exactly the surface the contract suite and J6's ACs demanded and stopped. Which is the same root as\n   [rebar:cc77-8120-bcc6-47e8]: nothing forced completeness.\n\nThe Approach now states the library-first rule AND warns about the JIRA-vs-Issue split explicitly, so\nthe next implementer does not repeat it a third time."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785481931701681001,"uuid":"842291aa-f78b-4ae8-8f4f-cba8e1a765f6"}